Ask each address family on its own in GETAI

The nscd protocol carries no address family, so glibc filters a GETAI
answer by the family the program asked for, and the answer has to hold
every family's addresses. nsncd made one lookup with no family to fill
it. systemd-resolved answers such a lookup of a .local name from
whichever of mDNS's IPv4 and IPv6 scopes replies first, with that
family's addresses alone, so on a machine whose neighbours answered over
IPv6 first, getent ahostsv4 and ssh -4 found nothing for a name
resolvectl resolved.

nsncd now asks for IPv6 and IPv4 at once, in two lookups on two threads,
and joins the answers; glibc sorts them afterwards. A lookup takes as
long as the slower of the two.

